1
00:00:01,293 --> 00:00:02,920
I JUST WALKED
IN THE BATHROOM

2
00:00:02,962 --> 00:00:04,421
AND SAW KATHY NAKED.

3
00:00:04,463 --> 00:00:06,340
IT WAS LIKE TORTURE.

4
00:00:06,381 --> 00:00:09,176
YOU KNOW, IF WE EVER GO
TO WAR AND YOU'RE CAPTURED

5
00:00:09,217 --> 00:00:10,928
YOU'RE IN FOR A BIG SURPRISE.

6
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,721
IT JUST KEEPS
GETTING WORSE.

7
00:00:12,763 --> 00:00:15,766
IT'S BAD ENOUGH THAT
I'M IN LOVE WITH MY
ROOMMATE'S GIRLFRIEND

8
00:00:15,808 --> 00:00:16,934
WHICH I THINK

9
00:00:16,976 --> 00:00:18,226
SHE KNOWS.

10
00:00:18,268 --> 00:00:20,312
EVERY TIME WE'RE
IN THE SAME ROOM TOGETHER

11
00:00:20,354 --> 00:00:22,063
THERE'S THIS WEIRD ENERGY
BETWEEN US.

12
00:00:22,105 --> 00:00:23,440
AND CALL ME CRAZY

13
00:00:23,482 --> 00:00:25,442
BUT I THINK
SHE LIKES ME, TOO.

14
00:00:25,484 --> 00:00:28,487
AND NOW...
I HAVE SEEN HER NAKED.

15
00:00:28,529 --> 00:00:30,948
AT LEAST, WHEN I'D SEEN HER
WITH CLOTHES ON

16
00:00:30,990 --> 00:00:32,783
I COULD IMAGINE THAT HER BODY

17
00:00:32,825 --> 00:00:34,117
WAS COVERED IN BOILS

18
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,410
OR SOMETHING.

19
00:00:35,452 --> 00:00:37,663
BUT THERE ARE NO BOILS.

20
00:00:37,705 --> 00:00:38,998
SHE'S SMOOTH.

21
00:00:40,666 --> 00:00:42,167
SMOOTH!

22
00:00:45,170 --> 00:00:46,254
WOW.

23
00:00:46,296 --> 00:00:48,256
COULD EVERYONE SEE UP HIS ROBE?

24
00:00:48,298 --> 00:00:50,300
YEAH, RIGHT
UP IT.
OH, MY GOD!

25
00:00:56,015 --> 00:01:00,811
♪ SO NO ONE TOLD YOU
LIFE WAS GONNA BE THIS WAY ♪

26
00:01:00,853 --> 00:01:03,313
♪ YOUR JOB'S A JOKE,
YOU'RE BROKE ♪

27
00:01:03,355 --> 00:01:05,691
♪ YOUR LOVE LIFE'S D.O.A. ♪

28
00:01:05,733 --> 00:01:10,654
♪ IT'S LIKE YOU'RE ALWAYS
STUCK IN SECOND GEAR ♪

29
00:01:10,696 --> 00:01:12,197
♪ WHEN IT HASN'T BEEN YOUR DAY ♪

30
00:01:12,239 --> 00:01:15,868
♪ YOUR WEEK, YOUR MONTH,
OR EVEN YOUR YEAR ♪

31
00:01:15,910 --> 00:01:19,705
♪ BUT I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

32
00:01:19,747 --> 00:01:22,041
♪ WHEN THE RAIN
STARTS TO POUR ♪

33
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:24,752
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

34
00:01:24,793 --> 00:01:27,379
♪ LIKE I'VE BEEN THERE BEFORE ♪

35
00:01:27,421 --> 00:01:29,297
♪ I'LL BE THERE FOR YOU ♪

36
00:01:29,339 --> 00:01:33,218
♪ 'CAUSE YOU'RE THERE
FOR ME, TOO. ♪

37
00:01:40,059 --> 00:01:41,100
GREAT. ALL RIGHT.

38
00:01:41,142 --> 00:01:42,937
SO I'LL
CALL YOU LATER.

39
00:01:44,103 --> 00:01:45,230
HEY, HEY, HEY.

40
00:01:45,272 --> 00:01:47,482
WHO WAS THAT?

41
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:48,609
THAT WOULD BE CACEY.

42
00:01:48,650 --> 00:01:49,944
WE'RE GOING OUT TONIGHT.

43
00:01:49,985 --> 00:01:51,236
GOING OUT, HUH?

44
00:01:51,278 --> 00:01:53,072
WOW! WOW!

45
00:01:54,281 --> 00:01:56,951
SO, THINGS DIDN'T WORK
OUT WITH KATHY, HUH?

46
00:01:56,992 --> 00:01:58,285
BUMMER.

47
00:01:58,326 --> 00:02:00,079
NO, THINGS ARE FINE
WITH KATHY.

48
00:02:00,119 --> 00:02:02,081
I'M HAVING A LATE DINNER
WITH HER TONIGHT

49
00:02:02,122 --> 00:02:03,122
RIGHT AFTER
MY EARLY DINNER

50
00:02:03,164 --> 00:02:04,666
WITH CACEY.

51
00:02:04,708 --> 00:02:06,125
WHAT?

52
00:02:06,167 --> 00:02:08,127
AND THE CRAZIEST THING IS
I JUST ATE A WHOLE PIZZA

53
00:02:08,169 --> 00:02:10,505
MYSELF.

54
00:02:10,547 --> 00:02:11,840
BUT...

55
00:02:11,882 --> 00:02:13,634
YOU'RE GOING OUT
WITH KATHY.

56
00:02:13,675 --> 00:02:14,760
YEAH.

57
00:02:14,802 --> 00:02:15,970
WHY ARE YOU UPSET?

58
00:02:16,011 --> 00:02:17,596
WELL, I'M UPSET...

59
00:02:17,638 --> 00:02:18,931
FOR YOU.

60
00:02:18,973 --> 00:02:20,390
YOU KNOW, I MEAN

61
00:02:20,432 --> 00:02:22,392
HAVING SEX WITH AN ENDLESS LINE
OF BEAUTIFUL WOMEN

62
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:23,644
MUST BE VERY UNFULFILLING

63
00:02:23,685 --> 00:02:24,686
FOR YOU.

64
00:02:26,354 --> 00:02:27,815
WHAT IS THE BIG DEAL?

65
00:02:27,856 --> 00:02:30,233
IT'S NOT LIKE
WE'RE EXCLUSIVE.

66
00:02:30,275 --> 00:02:32,235
LOOK, JOEY

67
00:02:32,277 --> 00:02:35,572
KATHY IS CLEARLY NOT FULFILLING
YOUR EMOTIONAL NEEDS

68
00:02:35,614 --> 00:02:36,991
BUT CACEY...

69
00:02:37,032 --> 00:02:39,868
I MEAN, GRANTED, I JUST SAW
THE BACK OF HER HEAD

70
00:02:39,910 --> 00:02:43,538
BUT I GOT THIS SENSE
THAT SHE'S SMART

71
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:46,625
AND FUNNY AND GETS YOU.

72
00:02:47,960 --> 00:02:50,253
YOU GOT ALL THAT FROM
THE BACK OF HER HEAD?

73
00:02:50,295 --> 00:02:52,631
I JUST THINK IT'S TIME
FOR YOU TO SETTLE DOWN--

74
00:02:52,673 --> 00:02:54,508
YOU KNOW, MAKE A CHOICE,
PICK A LANE.

75
00:02:54,549 --> 00:02:56,093
WHO'S ELAINE?

76
00:03:00,848 --> 00:03:02,599
♪ LITTLE TINY TARZAN ♪

77
00:03:02,641 --> 00:03:04,351
♪ SWINGING ON A NOSE HAIR ♪

78
00:03:04,392 --> 00:03:06,770
♪ SWINGING WITH THE
GREATEST OF EASE... ♪

79
00:03:06,812 --> 00:03:09,188
( clears throat, hums melody)

80
00:03:09,230 --> 00:03:12,026
DARN IT. I DON'T KNOW HOW
TO GET TO THE NEXT VERSE.

81
00:03:12,067 --> 00:03:15,194
YOU COULD JUST GO, UH...

82
00:03:15,236 --> 00:03:16,613
♪ GREATEST OF EASE ♪

83
00:03:16,655 --> 00:03:17,990
♪ BUM-A-NUMMA-NUMMA... ♪

84
00:03:18,032 --> 00:03:19,700
AND THEN GO RIGHT INTO IT.

85
00:03:19,741 --> 00:03:20,701
YEAH.

86
00:03:20,742 --> 00:03:22,161
OOH, I LIKE THAT.

87
00:03:22,201 --> 00:03:25,204
WAIT. HOW DO YOU KNOW
ABOUT "BUM-A-NUMMA-NUMMAS"?

88
00:03:25,246 --> 00:03:26,957
WELL, UH...

89
00:03:26,999 --> 00:03:28,959
YOU KNOW, I USED TO PLAY.

90
00:03:29,001 --> 00:03:30,711
OH, YEAH, THAT'S RIGHT.

91
00:03:30,752 --> 00:03:32,211
THE KEYBOARDS, HUH?

92
00:03:32,253 --> 00:03:34,213
YEAH. JUST A LITTLE
IN HIGH SCHOOL.

93
00:03:34,255 --> 00:03:36,508
I REALLY GOT INTO
IT IN COLLEGE.

94
00:03:36,550 --> 00:03:38,719
THAT'S WHEN I REALLY
FOUND MY SOUND.

95
00:03:38,760 --> 00:03:40,095
( chokes, laughs )

96
00:03:41,763 --> 00:03:44,224
OH, GOD. ORANGE JUICE
JUST CAME OUT OF MY NOSE

97
00:03:44,265 --> 00:03:45,767
BUT IT WAS
TOTALLY WORTH IT.

98
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:49,188
OH, MY GOD!

99
00:03:49,228 --> 00:03:51,356
I COMPLETELY FORGOT
ABOUT YOUR SOUND.

100
00:03:51,398 --> 00:03:53,025
YEAH.

101
00:03:53,067 --> 00:03:55,694
HE USED TO LOCK HIMSELF
IN THE BASEMENT FOR HOURS.

102
00:03:55,736 --> 00:03:59,531
NO ONE WAS EVER ALLOWED
TO HEAR "THE SOUND."

103
00:03:59,573 --> 00:04:02,034
I WANT TO HEAR "THE SOUND."

104
00:04:02,076 --> 00:04:04,119
NO. I MEAN...

105
00:04:04,161 --> 00:04:06,329
NO, I HAVEN'T PLAYED IN SO LONG

106
00:04:06,371 --> 00:04:07,915
AND, AND...

107
00:04:07,956 --> 00:04:10,667
WELL, IT'S REALLY
PERSONAL STUFF, YOU KNOW?

108
00:04:10,709 --> 00:04:13,128
COME ON. PLAY THAT FUNKY MUSIC,
WHITE BOY.

109
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:15,839
YEAH, COME ON.

110
00:04:15,881 --> 00:04:17,174
NO, YOU GUYS.

111
00:04:17,216 --> 00:04:20,219
MY KEYBOARDS ARE ALL THE WAY...
YEAH, OKAY.

112
00:04:27,142 --> 00:04:28,351
OKAY, GUYS.

113
00:04:28,393 --> 00:04:30,771
ALL RIGHT, BRING
IT ON, YOU.

114
00:04:33,148 --> 00:04:34,942
( clears throat )

115
00:04:34,983 --> 00:04:36,193
HERE WE GO.

116
00:04:38,153 --> 00:04:39,654
( inhales )

117
00:04:41,322 --> 00:04:42,449
( single note )

118
00:04:42,490 --> 00:04:45,744
YOU KNOW,
I'VE NEVER PLAYED MY STUFF

119
00:04:45,786 --> 00:04:47,246
FOR ANYONE BEFORE

120
00:04:47,287 --> 00:04:49,915
SO IT'S IMPORTANT
THAT YOU UNDERSTAND

121
00:04:49,957 --> 00:04:52,960
IT'S ABOUT COMMUNICATING...

122
00:04:53,001 --> 00:04:56,088
VERY PRIVATE EMOTIONS.

123
00:05:02,636 --> 00:05:03,929
YOU KNOW, UM...

124
00:05:03,971 --> 00:05:06,598
YOU SHOULD THINK OF, UM...

125
00:05:06,640 --> 00:05:08,308
MY WORK

126
00:05:08,349 --> 00:05:11,728
AS WORDLESS SOUND POEMS.

127
00:05:16,441 --> 00:05:17,567
THAT'S WHAT...

128
00:05:17,609 --> 00:05:19,069
OH, MY GOD. PLAY!

129
00:05:23,824 --> 00:05:25,993
( boogie woogie accompaniment)

130
00:05:26,034 --> 00:05:27,702
( dog barking )

131
00:05:29,412 --> 00:05:30,872
( cow mooing )

132
00:05:32,707 --> 00:05:35,252
( rooster crows, dog barks )

133
00:05:35,294 --> 00:05:36,795
( buzzing )

134
00:05:36,837 --> 00:05:38,797
( doorbell ringing )

135
00:05:38,839 --> 00:05:41,175
( laser zapping )

136
00:05:41,216 --> 00:05:43,051
( rattling )

137
00:05:43,093 --> 00:05:48,307
( explosion )

138
00:05:54,021 --> 00:05:56,523
BOY, YOU KNOW,
TH-THAT WAS, UH...

139
00:05:58,025 --> 00:05:59,318
TERRIFIC.

140
00:06:00,819 --> 00:06:02,863
REALLY...

141
00:06:02,904 --> 00:06:04,447
BITCHIN'.

142
00:06:06,325 --> 00:06:07,492
WOW!

143
00:06:07,534 --> 00:06:09,828
IT WAS SO... WOW!

144
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,330
REALLY? I MEAN, REALLY?

145
00:06:11,370 --> 00:06:12,873
OH, YEAH!

146
00:06:12,914 --> 00:06:16,375
I MEAN, YOU SHOULD...
PLAY IN PUBLIC.

147
00:06:16,417 --> 00:06:18,753
WOW! THANKS, YOU GUYS!

148
00:06:18,795 --> 00:06:20,088
THAT'S, OH...

149
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:22,341
OH, I WANT TO PLAY YOU
ANOTHER PIECE.

150
00:06:22,381 --> 00:06:23,967
UM... OH!

151
00:06:24,009 --> 00:06:27,512
I LEFT MY HELICOPTER SOUNDS
ON ANOTHER DISK.

152
00:06:27,554 --> 00:06:29,264
I'LL BE RIGHT BACK, OKAY?

153
00:06:29,306 --> 00:06:30,974
OH, THIS IS...

154
00:06:31,016 --> 00:06:32,517
THIS IS SO NICE.

155
00:06:32,559 --> 00:06:34,393
I MEAN, I AM SO...

156
00:06:39,024 --> 00:06:42,443
OH, GOD BLESS MY DAD
FOR SOUNDPROOFING THE BASEMENT.

157
00:06:43,904 --> 00:06:47,282
I CAN'T BELIEVE I EVER LET HIM
TOUCH ME WITH THOSE FINGERS.

158
00:06:49,034 --> 00:06:50,369
WHAT ARE YOU
TALKING ABOUT?

159
00:06:50,409 --> 00:06:52,371
I LOVED IT!

160
00:06:52,411 --> 00:06:54,915
IT WAS SO MOVING.

161
00:06:54,956 --> 00:06:56,666
PLUS, IT'S SO DIFFERENT

162
00:06:56,708 --> 00:06:58,668
FROM THE STUFF
YOU USUALLY HEAR.

163
00:06:58,710 --> 00:07:00,087
YOU MEAN MUSIC?

164
00:07:04,216 --> 00:07:05,717
( quacking )

165
00:07:05,759 --> 00:07:07,552
YEAH, I KNOW
WHAT YOU'RE THINKING.

166
00:07:07,594 --> 00:07:11,765
YES, YES. YOUR BREASTS
ARE JUST AS FIRM AND JUICY.

167
00:07:11,806 --> 00:07:13,474
( knocking )

168
00:07:13,516 --> 00:07:15,894
COME IN.

169
00:07:15,936 --> 00:07:17,229
HEY.

170
00:07:17,271 --> 00:07:19,606
OH, GOD. IS THAT BAYWATCH?

171
00:07:19,647 --> 00:07:23,151
UH, YES, BUT, UH, I JUST
WATCH IT FOR THE ARTICLES.

172
00:07:23,193 --> 00:07:25,486
SO, IS JOEY AROUND?

173
00:07:25,528 --> 00:07:28,615
NO. HE'S NOT BACK YET, BUT HE'S
GOING TO BE HERE ANY MINUTE.

174
00:07:28,656 --> 00:07:30,325
HAVE A SEAT. BOW OR STERN?

175
00:07:30,367 --> 00:07:32,619
I DON'T REALLY HAVE
A PREFERENCE. YOU?

176
00:07:32,660 --> 00:07:34,829
WELL, I LIKE IT IN THE STERN.

177
00:07:37,332 --> 00:07:39,126
OF THE BOAT.

178
00:07:39,167 --> 00:07:41,086
( phone rings )

179
00:07:41,128 --> 00:07:42,296
HELLO.

180
00:07:42,337 --> 00:07:43,671
HEY, IT'S ME.

181
00:07:43,713 --> 00:07:46,258
LISTEN, CACEY AND I HAD
A LITTLE CAR TROUBLE.

182
00:07:46,300 --> 00:07:47,259
WHAT HAPPENED?

183
00:07:47,301 --> 00:07:48,260
We broke down

184
00:07:48,302 --> 00:07:49,469
ON THE PARKWAY.

185
00:07:49,510 --> 00:07:51,305
I HAVE TO GET
SOME TRANSMISSION FLUID.

186
00:07:51,346 --> 00:07:54,515
COULD YOU PLEASE TELL KATHY I'M
SORRY AND I'LL BE THERE SOON?

187
00:07:54,557 --> 00:07:56,184
WHY CAN'T YOU TELL HER?

188
00:07:56,226 --> 00:07:59,520
'Cause I only have one quarter
and my time is about to...

189
00:07:59,562 --> 00:08:01,148
JOEY? JOEY?

190
00:08:01,189 --> 00:08:02,690
YEAH?

191
00:08:04,567 --> 00:08:06,527
I THOUGHT YOUR TIME RAN OUT.

192
00:08:06,569 --> 00:08:09,239
ME, TOO, BUT I GUESS
I DO HAVE A COUPLE OF...

193
00:08:10,698 --> 00:08:13,327
UH, THAT WAS JOEY.

194
00:08:13,368 --> 00:08:15,870
HE'S RUNNING A LITTLE LATE
AND HE SAYS HE'S SORRY.

195
00:08:15,912 --> 00:08:18,332
SO I GUESS IT'S JUST
YOU AND ME, THEN.

196
00:08:18,373 --> 00:08:20,667
OH. OKAY.

197
00:08:20,708 --> 00:08:22,627
YEAH. I THINK IT IS.

198
00:08:25,880 --> 00:08:27,715
SO, WHAT DID YOU DO TODAY?

199
00:08:27,757 --> 00:08:29,884
I HAD AN APPOINTMENT
TO GET MY HAIR CUT...

200
00:08:29,926 --> 00:08:30,760
IT LOOKS GREAT.

201
00:08:30,802 --> 00:08:32,971
AND THEN IT GOT CANCELED.

202
00:08:34,306 --> 00:08:35,849
WELL, I COULD CUT IT.

203
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:37,392
REALLY? DO YOU DO THAT?

204
00:08:37,434 --> 00:08:38,726
YEAH, I DO.

205
00:08:38,768 --> 00:08:40,854
I LEARNED IT IN MY AUNT'S
DOG-GROOMING SHOP

206
00:08:40,895 --> 00:08:42,439
BUT WHAT DO YOU SAY?

207
00:08:42,481 --> 00:08:44,316
DOG-GROOMING, HUH?

208
00:08:44,358 --> 00:08:46,985
OKAY, JUST DON'T MAKE
MY TAIL TOO POOFY.

209
00:08:52,782 --> 00:08:55,327
YOU HAVE
REALLY GREAT HAIR.

210
00:08:55,369 --> 00:08:56,577
WELL, THANKS.

211
00:08:56,619 --> 00:08:58,079
I GROW IT MYSELF.

212
00:08:59,247 --> 00:09:00,374
MMM!

213
00:09:00,415 --> 00:09:02,083
MMM!

214
00:09:02,125 --> 00:09:03,710
MMM...

215
00:09:03,751 --> 00:09:06,046
YOU KNOW WHO ALSO
HAS GREAT HAIR IS JOEY.

216
00:09:06,087 --> 00:09:08,173
YES. YEAH, JOEY
HAS GREAT HAIR.

217
00:09:08,215 --> 00:09:10,550
UM, I'M BASICALLY
DONE HERE.

218
00:09:10,591 --> 00:09:12,969
LET ME JUST GET
THIS HAIR OFF YOUR NECK.

219
00:09:25,648 --> 00:09:28,068
WH-WHAT'RE YOU DOING?

220
00:09:28,109 --> 00:09:30,820
CHECKING TO SEE
IF IT'S EVEN.

221
00:09:30,862 --> 00:09:32,947
'KAY.

222
00:09:35,409 --> 00:09:36,826
IT LOOKS GOOD.

223
00:09:38,412 --> 00:09:39,704
( phone ringing )

224
00:09:39,746 --> 00:09:41,039
IT'S THE PHONE!

225
00:09:41,081 --> 00:09:43,124
THE PHONE'S MAKING SOUNDS!

226
00:09:43,166 --> 00:09:44,501
HELLO.

227
00:09:44,543 --> 00:09:45,919
HEY, DUDE, IT'S ME.

228
00:09:45,960 --> 00:09:47,128
HEY, IT'S JOEY.

229
00:09:47,170 --> 00:09:48,463
OH.

230
00:09:48,505 --> 00:09:50,589
WE'RE GOING TO BE STUCK HERE
FOR A WHILE.

231
00:09:50,631 --> 00:09:53,427
I GOT THE TRANSMISSION FLUID,
WENT TO PUT IT IN THE CAR--

232
00:09:53,468 --> 00:09:54,844
THE TRANSMISSION WASN'T THERE.

233
00:09:54,886 --> 00:09:55,970
WHAT?

234
00:09:56,012 --> 00:09:57,305
It must've fallen out

235
00:09:57,347 --> 00:09:58,432
A FEW BLOCKS BACK.

236
00:09:58,473 --> 00:09:59,933
I FIGURED WE HIT A DOG.

237
00:09:59,974 --> 00:10:01,851
OH. OKAY.

238
00:10:01,893 --> 00:10:03,603
Could you put Kathy on?

239
00:10:03,644 --> 00:10:05,646
I want to apologize to her.

240
00:10:05,688 --> 00:10:08,191
OH. YEAH, MAN. JOEY.

241
00:10:08,233 --> 00:10:09,526
HEY.

242
00:10:09,568 --> 00:10:10,985
OH, NO. IT'S FINE.

243
00:10:11,027 --> 00:10:12,820
DON'T WORRY ABOUT IT.

244
00:10:12,862 --> 00:10:14,531
NO, STOP APOLOGIZING.

245
00:10:14,573 --> 00:10:15,865
IT'S OKAY.

246
00:10:15,907 --> 00:10:17,742
YEAH. I'LL TALK
TO YOU TOMORROW.

247
00:10:20,745 --> 00:10:22,997
I SHOULD, UH,
PROBABLY GO.

248
00:10:23,039 --> 00:10:25,166
YEAH. YES. YEAH.

249
00:10:33,341 --> 00:10:34,884
( knock at door )

250
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,973
I FORGOT MY PURSE.

251
00:10:40,014 --> 00:10:41,349
OH.

252
00:10:47,230 --> 00:10:48,398
OH! I REALLY DID.

253
00:10:48,440 --> 00:10:49,690
I FORGOT MY PURSE.

254
00:10:49,732 --> 00:10:51,109
( mumbling
incoherently )

255
00:10:55,614 --> 00:10:56,697
OH, NO!

256
00:10:56,739 --> 00:10:58,366
THIS IS BAD, IT'S BAD.
THIS IS BAD.

257
00:10:58,408 --> 00:10:59,659
HORRIBLE.

258
00:10:59,700 --> 00:11:02,787
WAIT, THE, UH, THE KISS,
OR THE SITUATION?

259
00:11:02,829 --> 00:11:04,872
NO, THE KISS WAS GOOD.

260
00:11:04,914 --> 00:11:05,957
NO, BUT THAT'S BAD!

261
00:11:05,999 --> 00:11:07,792
OH, YES!
OKAY, HERE'S WHAT WE DO.

262
00:11:07,834 --> 00:11:09,043
WE FORGET IT HAPPENED.

263
00:11:09,085 --> 00:11:09,961
WHAT?

264
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,338
WE SWALLOW OUR FEELINGS

265
00:11:11,379 --> 00:11:13,632
EVEN IF IT MEANS
WE'RE UNHAPPY FOREVER.

266
00:11:13,672 --> 00:11:14,673
SOUND GOOD?

267
00:11:15,716 --> 00:11:17,885
CAN YOU REALLY DO THAT?

268
00:11:17,927 --> 00:11:18,886
I HAVE TO.

269
00:11:18,928 --> 00:11:21,055
HE'S MY BEST FRIEND...

270
00:11:21,097 --> 00:11:23,266
AND YOU'RE SEEING HIM.

271
00:11:23,308 --> 00:11:26,520
OH, CHANDLER, I LIKE JOEY A LOT

272
00:11:26,561 --> 00:11:28,188
BUT WITH YOU...

273
00:11:28,229 --> 00:11:29,856
OH, NO, NO, DON'T. SEE?

274
00:11:29,897 --> 00:11:32,025
SEE, YOU'RE GETTING ME CONFUSED.

275
00:11:32,066 --> 00:11:33,568
I'M STARTING TO YEARN.

276
00:11:36,571 --> 00:11:38,323
I'M SORRY.

277
00:11:38,365 --> 00:11:40,699
IF YOU WANT TO PRETEND
THAT NOTHING HAPPENED

278
00:11:40,741 --> 00:11:42,827
I CAN TRY.

279
00:11:42,869 --> 00:11:46,247
I-I THINK WE HAVE TO.

280
00:11:47,290 --> 00:11:50,377
OKAY.

281
00:11:50,418 --> 00:11:51,586
BYE.

282
00:11:51,628 --> 00:11:52,711
BYE.

283
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:55,923
( door opens and shuts )

284
00:12:02,889 --> 00:12:05,724
ARE YOU STILL OUT THERE?

285
00:12:05,766 --> 00:12:07,810
NO.

286
00:12:13,732 --> 00:12:15,943
( shrill, abrasive
synthesizer melodies )

287
00:12:15,985 --> 00:12:18,821
( distorted):
ELECTRIFYING...

288
00:12:20,823 --> 00:12:23,117
INFINITE TIME...

289
00:12:23,159 --> 00:12:25,453
( echoing ):
TIME... TIME... TIME...

290
00:12:25,495 --> 00:12:29,082
YOU KNOW, THERE'S
A STARBUCKS ABOUT
THREE BLOCKS DOWN.

291
00:12:29,123 --> 00:12:30,500
HE'S SO INSPIRED.

292
00:12:30,542 --> 00:12:31,918
JUST LOOK AT HIM.

293
00:12:31,959 --> 00:12:33,169
LOOK AT HIM GO.

294
00:12:33,211 --> 00:12:35,338
( spacy noodling )

295
00:12:35,380 --> 00:12:37,382
( clock ticking )

296
00:12:40,218 --> 00:12:44,347
( explosion )

297
00:12:45,724 --> 00:12:49,018
( polite applause )

298
00:12:49,060 --> 00:12:52,188
( distorted echo ):
THANK YOU, NEW YORK...
NEW YORK... NEW YORK...

299
00:12:52,230 --> 00:12:55,483
HEY, AREN'T
YOU UP NEXT?

300
00:12:55,525 --> 00:12:58,194
OH, NO.
I'M NOT PLAYING TONIGHT.

301
00:12:58,236 --> 00:12:59,195
WHY NOT?

302
00:12:59,237 --> 00:13:02,198
I CAN'T FOLLOW ROSS.

303
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,950
ARE YOU KIDDING?

304
00:13:03,991 --> 00:13:06,869
THAT WOULD BE LIKE THOSE
POOR BICYCLE-RIDING CHIMPS

305
00:13:06,911 --> 00:13:09,872
WHO HAD TO FOLLOW
THE BEATLES. NO.

306
00:13:09,914 --> 00:13:13,126
PHOEBE, ROSS SUCKS.

307
00:13:14,168 --> 00:13:16,588
PHOEBE,
THE PLACE HAS EMPTIED

308
00:13:16,630 --> 00:13:17,964
BECAUSE OF HIM.

309
00:13:18,005 --> 00:13:20,216
OH, MY GOD,
HE'S NOT EVEN APPRECIATED

310
00:13:20,258 --> 00:13:22,302
IN HIS OWN TIME.

311
00:13:22,343 --> 00:13:23,553
I WOULD GIVE ANYTHING

312
00:13:23,595 --> 00:13:26,389
TO NOT BE APPRECIATED
IN MY OWN TIME!

313
00:13:28,849 --> 00:13:31,269
OKAY. UM, PHOEBE...

314
00:13:32,312 --> 00:13:34,897
YOU SUCK, TOO.

315
00:13:37,066 --> 00:13:39,986
YEAH, PHOEBE, YOU'RE...

316
00:13:40,027 --> 00:13:41,362
AWFUL!

317
00:13:44,198 --> 00:13:46,867
YOU GUYS.

318
00:13:46,909 --> 00:13:49,245
"YEAH, YOU SUCK, TOO."

319
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:54,626
OH, MAN!

320
00:13:54,668 --> 00:13:59,172
I CAN'T BELIEVE
I LOCKED MYSELF OUT AGAIN!

321
00:13:59,213 --> 00:14:01,758
HANG ON, BUDDY.

322
00:14:05,219 --> 00:14:06,179
OH, MY GOD.

323
00:14:06,220 --> 00:14:07,305
WHAT HAPPENED HERE?

324
00:14:07,347 --> 00:14:08,431
DID YOU DO ALL THIS?

325
00:14:08,473 --> 00:14:09,432
I SURE DID.

326
00:14:09,474 --> 00:14:10,767
WHY?

327
00:14:10,809 --> 00:14:12,686
I JUST THOUGHT
IT WOULD MAKE ME FEEL GOOD

328
00:14:12,727 --> 00:14:14,437
TO DO SOMETHING NICE
FOR MY FRIEND.

329
00:14:14,479 --> 00:14:16,022
YOU'RE AMAZING.

330
00:14:16,063 --> 00:14:17,190
NO, NO, NO.

331
00:14:17,231 --> 00:14:19,776
THIS IS AMAZING.

332
00:14:21,902 --> 00:14:23,946
A TV THAT APPEARS
AS IF FROM NOWHERE!

333
00:14:25,198 --> 00:14:26,741
THAT'S THE DREAM!

334
00:14:28,034 --> 00:14:29,868
HOW DID YOU
AFFORD ALL THIS STUFF?!

335
00:14:29,910 --> 00:14:31,204
WELL, YOU KNOW, I'M 29.

336
00:14:31,245 --> 00:14:33,122
I MEAN,
WHO NEEDS A SAVINGS ACCOUNT?

337
00:14:33,164 --> 00:14:36,083
YOU ARE THE BEST FRIEND
ANYONE HAS EVER HAD.

338
00:14:36,125 --> 00:14:38,252
OH, I DON'T KNOW.

339
00:14:38,294 --> 00:14:40,380
NO, NO, NO, YOU ARE.

340
00:14:40,421 --> 00:14:43,007
YOU DO THIS, YOU GIVE
ME THE GREAT ADVICE

341
00:14:43,049 --> 00:14:45,719
AND LISTEN, I WAS
THINKING ABOUT WHAT
YOU SAID YESTERDAY

342
00:14:45,760 --> 00:14:47,220
ABOUT FOCUSING
ON ONE WOMAN?

343
00:14:47,261 --> 00:14:48,388
I'M GOING TO DO THAT.

344
00:14:48,429 --> 00:14:49,848
YOU MEAN WITH CACEY?

345
00:14:49,889 --> 00:14:52,433
NO. I THINK I'LL SEE
HOW THINGS GO WITH KATHY.

346
00:14:52,475 --> 00:14:53,434
SHE'S PRETTY COOL.

347
00:14:53,476 --> 00:14:54,435
OR CACEY.

348
00:14:54,477 --> 00:14:55,603
NO, NO, KATHY.

349
00:14:55,645 --> 00:14:57,230
COULD BE CACEY.

350
00:14:57,271 --> 00:14:58,523
NO, NO, KATHY.

351
00:14:58,565 --> 00:14:59,691
CONSIDER CACEY.

352
00:15:00,692 --> 00:15:02,109
YOU KNOW WHAT I THINK?

353
00:15:02,151 --> 00:15:03,277
I THINK SOMEBODY'S

354
00:15:03,319 --> 00:15:05,238
GOT A LITTLE
CRUSH ON CACEY.

355
00:15:05,279 --> 00:15:07,156
HOW ABOUT I
FIX YOU TWO UP?

356
00:15:07,198 --> 00:15:08,616
WHAT DO YOU THINK?

357
00:15:08,658 --> 00:15:10,535
THAT ALL THE PIECES
OF MY LIFE

358
00:15:10,577 --> 00:15:12,537
ARE FALLING
RIGHT INTO PLACE.

359
00:15:20,294 --> 00:15:21,254
HEY.

360
00:15:21,295 --> 00:15:22,921
HEY, YOU WERE
REALLY GREAT.

361
00:15:22,963 --> 00:15:24,841
YOU WERE REALLY,
REALLY GREAT.

362
00:15:24,883 --> 00:15:25,842
THANKS.

363
00:15:25,884 --> 00:15:27,968
THANKS.

364
00:15:28,010 --> 00:15:29,303
SO, MONICA TELLS ME

365
00:15:29,345 --> 00:15:32,098
THAT, UH, YOU DON'T
WANT TO PLAY ANYMORE

366
00:15:32,139 --> 00:15:33,099
BECAUSE OF ME

367
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:36,644
AND, YOU KNOW,
MY TALENT.

368
00:15:36,686 --> 00:15:37,771
IS THAT TRUE?

369
00:15:37,812 --> 00:15:38,938
WELL...

370
00:15:38,979 --> 00:15:40,523
KIND OF, YEAH. YEAH.

371
00:15:40,565 --> 00:15:41,566
PHEEBS...

372
00:15:41,608 --> 00:15:43,401
YEAH, I MEAN, YOU KNOW

373
00:15:43,443 --> 00:15:46,821
AND I WAS TRYING TO BE
REALLY, YOU KNOW, OKAY
AND UPBEAT ABOUT IT

374
00:15:46,863 --> 00:15:49,449
BUT I FEEL SO...
DWARFED BY YOUR MUSICAL GIFT.

375
00:15:49,490 --> 00:15:51,284
I...

376
00:15:51,325 --> 00:15:53,119
SEE, BUT PHEEBS

377
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:55,830
THAT IS THE EXACT
OPPOSITE INTENT

378
00:15:55,872 --> 00:15:57,707
OF MY MUSIC.

379
00:15:57,749 --> 00:16:00,959
MY MUSIC IS MEANT
TO INSPIRE

380
00:16:01,001 --> 00:16:02,962
AND IF IT BOTHERS
YOU THIS MUCH

381
00:16:03,003 --> 00:16:05,632
THEN I...

382
00:16:05,673 --> 00:16:07,049
I WON'T PLAY ANYMORE.

383
00:16:08,509 --> 00:16:09,469
OH, NO.

384
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,969
NO, NO, NO.
DON'T DO THAT.

385
00:16:11,011 --> 00:16:12,806
HOW COULD I LIVE
WITH MYSELF

386
00:16:12,847 --> 00:16:16,517
IF I KNEW I WAS DEPRIVING
THE WORLD OF YOUR MUSIC?

387
00:16:18,394 --> 00:16:20,187
YEAH, OKAY.

388
00:16:26,736 --> 00:16:28,988
SAW THE NEW
FURNITURE.

389
00:16:29,029 --> 00:16:30,364
VERY NICE.

390
00:16:30,406 --> 00:16:32,742
YEAH, JOEY HAS THE
BEST BOYFRIEND EVER.

391
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:36,704
I KISSED KATHY.

392
00:16:36,746 --> 00:16:38,289
MY GOD!
ARE YOU SERIOUS?

393
00:16:38,331 --> 00:16:39,332
DOES JOEY KNOW?

394
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:40,333
NO.

395
00:16:40,374 --> 00:16:41,626
IS THERE ANY WAY--

396
00:16:41,668 --> 00:16:44,337
ANY WAY YOU THINK HE
WILL UNDERSTAND THIS?

397
00:16:44,378 --> 00:16:46,380
YOU OBVIOUSLY
HAVEN'T SCREWED OVER

398
00:16:46,422 --> 00:16:47,715
A LOT OF YOUR FRIENDS.

399
00:16:48,675 --> 00:16:50,802
WHICH WE ALL APPRECIATE.

400
00:16:50,844 --> 00:16:52,470
YOU KNOW, THE SAD THING IS

401
00:16:52,512 --> 00:16:55,348
IF YOU HAD TOLD HIM HOW YOU
FELT BEFORE YOU KISSED HER

402
00:16:55,389 --> 00:16:58,351
KNOWING JOEY, HE PROBABLY
JUST WOULD'VE STEPPED ASIDE.

403
00:16:58,392 --> 00:16:59,727
OH, DON'T SAY THAT.

404
00:16:59,769 --> 00:17:00,854
DON'T SAY THAT.

405
00:17:00,895 --> 00:17:02,563
THAT'S NOT TRUE, IS IT?

406
00:17:02,605 --> 00:17:04,357
YEAH.
HE LOVES YOU.
YEAH.

407
00:17:04,398 --> 00:17:07,193
WELL, WHY DIDN'T YOU
TELL ME TO DO THAT?!

408
00:17:07,234 --> 00:17:08,194
I DON'T KNOW.

409
00:17:08,235 --> 00:17:09,779
I-I SAID SOMETHING
TO PHOEBE.

410
00:17:09,821 --> 00:17:12,657
THAT'S RIGHT, AND I THOUGHT
IT WAS A REALLY GOOD IDEA.

411
00:17:12,699 --> 00:17:13,700
YEAH, I REMEMBER.

412
00:17:13,741 --> 00:17:14,701
YOU DID.

413
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:15,869
OH, MY GOD!

414
00:17:15,910 --> 00:17:17,203
WHAT AM I GOING TO DO?

415
00:17:17,244 --> 00:17:18,287
WELL, CHANDLER

416
00:17:18,329 --> 00:17:20,164
YOU'RE GOING
TO HAVE TO TELL HIM.

417
00:17:20,206 --> 00:17:21,916
WHY? WHY DO I HAVE TO TELL HIM?

418
00:17:21,958 --> 00:17:23,083
BECAUSE YOU DO.

419
00:17:23,125 --> 00:17:24,878
YEAH, I KNOW.

420
00:17:25,920 --> 00:17:28,088
HEY.

421
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:31,050
WOULD IT BE OKAY IF I WROTE
A SONG ABOUT THIS?

422
00:17:37,348 --> 00:17:38,307
HEY.

423
00:17:38,349 --> 00:17:39,308
HEY.

424
00:17:39,350 --> 00:17:40,643
Wonder Woman:
Steve...?

425
00:17:40,685 --> 00:17:41,811
SAMBUCA MARGARITA?

426
00:17:41,853 --> 00:17:42,812
Are you here?

427
00:17:42,854 --> 00:17:44,397
IS THAT A REAL THING?

428
00:17:44,438 --> 00:17:47,483
WELL, WE ONLY HAD
SAMBUCA, SO IT IS NOW.

429
00:17:47,525 --> 00:17:49,819
LISTEN, UH, JOE, I-I NEED TO--

430
00:17:49,861 --> 00:17:52,446
I NEED TO TALK TO YOU
ABOUT SOMETHING.

431
00:17:52,488 --> 00:17:54,866
WHAT'S UP?

432
00:17:54,908 --> 00:17:55,992
( clearing throat )

433
00:17:56,034 --> 00:17:57,660
IT'S, IT'S ABOUT KATHY.

434
00:17:57,702 --> 00:17:59,286
UM...

435
00:17:59,328 --> 00:18:00,287
UH...

436
00:18:00,329 --> 00:18:01,581
I LIKE HER.

437
00:18:01,622 --> 00:18:04,709
I LIKE HER A LOT, ACTUALLY.

438
00:18:04,751 --> 00:18:06,627
YOU DO?

439
00:18:06,669 --> 00:18:08,254
YEAH.

440
00:18:08,295 --> 00:18:10,423
WELL, YOUR TIMING
COULDN'T BE BETTER

441
00:18:10,464 --> 00:18:12,717
'CAUSE SHE'S NOT MY
GIRLFRIEND ANYMORE.

442
00:18:12,759 --> 00:18:14,052
WHAT?

443
00:18:14,092 --> 00:18:16,220
YEAH, SHE BROKE
UP WITH ME.

444
00:18:16,262 --> 00:18:18,765
OH, UH... WHEN?

445
00:18:18,806 --> 00:18:20,474
JUST NOW,
AFTER ACTING CLASS.

446
00:18:20,516 --> 00:18:23,436
AT FIRST, I THOUGHT SHE WAS
DOING SOME KIND OF SCENE.

447
00:18:23,477 --> 00:18:25,187
THAT'S WHY I LET
PEOPLE WATCH.

448
00:18:25,229 --> 00:18:27,857
OH... MAN, I AM SO SORRY.

449
00:18:27,899 --> 00:18:30,651
ARE YOU, ARE-ARE YOU OKAY?

450
00:18:30,693 --> 00:18:33,780
I'VE BEEN BETTER, YOU
KNOW, BUT I'M ALL RIGHT.

451
00:18:33,821 --> 00:18:35,114
SO, YOU LIKE HER, HUH?

452
00:18:35,155 --> 00:18:36,950
YES, BUT I, I,
I DON'T HAVE TO.

453
00:18:36,991 --> 00:18:37,951
NO, NO, NO.

454
00:18:37,992 --> 00:18:39,452
IT'S, UH...

455
00:18:39,493 --> 00:18:40,828
IT'S OKAY.

456
00:18:40,870 --> 00:18:42,329
YEAH?

457
00:18:42,371 --> 00:18:43,748
YEAH.

458
00:18:43,790 --> 00:18:45,083
YOU KNOW WHY?

459
00:18:45,124 --> 00:18:47,334
'CAUSE YOU CAME TO ME FIRST.

460
00:18:49,420 --> 00:18:52,924
WELL, I THOUGHT THAT WOULD BE
THE BEST THING TO DO.

461
00:18:52,966 --> 00:18:55,051
BUT, HEY, LISTEN,
JUST SO YOU KNOW--

462
00:18:55,093 --> 00:18:56,552
YOU MIGHT HAVE YOUR
WORK CUT OUT FOR YOU

463
00:18:56,594 --> 00:18:58,262
BECAUSE WHEN I
TALKED TO HER

464
00:18:58,304 --> 00:18:59,346
I KIND OF
GOT THE FEELING

465
00:18:59,388 --> 00:19:02,934
SHE'S INTO SOME
OTHER GUY, SO...

466
00:19:02,976 --> 00:19:04,143
SEE, UH, THAT'S,
THAT'S ACTUALLY

467
00:19:04,184 --> 00:19:06,854
WHAT I WANTED
TO TALK TO YOU ABOUT.

468
00:19:06,896 --> 00:19:10,733
I-I THINK I KNOW
WHO THE OTHER GUY IS.

469
00:19:10,775 --> 00:19:12,819
WHO?

470
00:19:12,860 --> 00:19:15,237
IT'S ME.

471
00:19:15,279 --> 00:19:17,448
I'M THE OTHER GUY.

472
00:19:17,490 --> 00:19:20,118
WHAT?

473
00:19:20,158 --> 00:19:22,996
YEAH, I MEAN,
WHEN YOU WERE LATE LAST NIGHT

474
00:19:23,037 --> 00:19:25,289
KATHY AND I GOT TO TALKING
AND...

475
00:19:25,331 --> 00:19:28,167
ONE THING LED TO ANOTHER AND...

476
00:19:28,208 --> 00:19:29,460
AND WHAT?

477
00:19:29,502 --> 00:19:30,837
DID YOU SLEEP WITH HER?

478
00:19:30,878 --> 00:19:32,672
NO! NO, NO, I JUST KISSED HER.

479
00:19:32,713 --> 00:19:34,966
WHAT?! THAT'S EVEN WORSE!

480
00:19:35,008 --> 00:19:36,634
HOW IS THAT WORSE?!

481
00:19:36,676 --> 00:19:38,636
I DON'T KNOW,
BUT IT'S THE SAME!

482
00:19:38,678 --> 00:19:42,264
ALL RIGHT, LOOK, I'M
SORRY, BUT THERE WAS
NOTHING I COULD DO.

483
00:19:42,306 --> 00:19:44,433
I THINK I'M IN
LOVE WITH HER.

484
00:19:44,475 --> 00:19:46,310
WHO CARES!
YOU WENT BEHIND MY BACK?!

485
00:19:46,352 --> 00:19:47,728
I'D NEVER DO THAT TO YOU!

486
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:48,729
YOU'RE RIGHT.

487
00:19:48,771 --> 00:19:49,730
I HAVE NO EXCUSES.

488
00:19:49,772 --> 00:19:51,315
I WAS TOTALLY OVER THE LINE.

489
00:19:51,357 --> 00:19:52,566
"OVER THE LINE?"

490
00:19:52,608 --> 00:19:54,694
Y-Y-YOU'RE,
YOU'RE SO FAR PAST THE LINE

491
00:19:54,735 --> 00:19:56,529
THAT YOU CAN'T EVEN SEE
THE LINE!

492
00:19:56,570 --> 00:19:58,072
THE LINE IS A DOT TO YOU.

493
00:19:58,114 --> 00:19:59,157
YES.

494
00:19:59,197 --> 00:20:01,034
YES, RIGHT, AND
I FEEL HORRIBLE.

495
00:20:01,075 --> 00:20:03,036
YOU HAVE TO BELIEVE ME.

496
00:20:03,077 --> 00:20:04,286
OH, MY GOD.

497
00:20:04,328 --> 00:20:06,747
IS THAT WHY
YOU BOUGHT ALL THIS STUFF?!

498
00:20:08,374 --> 00:20:09,959
WELL, YOU KNOW WHAT?

499
00:20:10,001 --> 00:20:13,129
I WILL NOT WATCH YOUR TV,
I WILL NOT LISTEN TO YOUR STEREO

500
00:20:13,171 --> 00:20:16,423
AND THERE'S A CINNAMON RAISIN
LOAF IN THE NEW BREAD MAKER

501
00:20:16,465 --> 00:20:18,009
THAT I'M NOT GOING TO EAT!

502
00:20:18,051 --> 00:20:19,010
YOU KNOW WHY?

503
00:20:19,052 --> 00:20:20,136
PROBABLY BECAUSE...

504
00:20:20,178 --> 00:20:21,679
BECAUSE IT'S ALL TAINTED

505
00:20:21,721 --> 00:20:22,930
WITH YOUR BETRAYAL.

506
00:20:24,306 --> 00:20:27,060
FROM NOW ON,
THIS APARTMENT IS EMPTY TO ME

507
00:20:27,101 --> 00:20:29,436
AND I'M NOT HAPPY
ABOUT YOU EITHER.

508
00:20:33,399 --> 00:20:34,901
( bread maker ringing )

509
00:20:34,942 --> 00:20:37,737
OH, AND JUST SO YOU KNOW.

510
00:20:37,778 --> 00:20:40,740
I MADE THAT BREAD FOR YOU.

511
00:20:42,408 --> 00:20:45,494
( door slams )

512
00:20:50,583 --> 00:20:52,251
( rooster crows )

513
00:20:52,292 --> 00:20:54,795
( doorbell buzzes )

514
00:20:54,837 --> 00:20:56,589
OH, MY GOD,
HE'S LOST IT.

515
00:20:56,630 --> 00:20:57,965
HE'S TOTALLY LOST IT.

516
00:20:59,425 --> 00:21:00,384
WHAT?

517
00:21:00,426 --> 00:21:02,261
PHOEBE, THIS IS MUSIC

518
00:21:02,302 --> 00:21:04,013
THAT CANNOT GET ANY WORSE.

519
00:21:04,055 --> 00:21:07,225
THERE ARE RATS IN THE BASEMENT
THAT ARE HANGING THEMSELVES.

520
00:21:08,601 --> 00:21:11,562
( explosion )

521
00:21:17,484 --> 00:21:18,444
THANK YOU.

522
00:21:18,485 --> 00:21:19,486
THANKS.

523
00:21:22,865 --> 00:21:24,700
YEAH, I LOST IT.

524
00:21:26,326 --> 00:21:28,328
YOU KNOW, I'M
NOT GOING TO
PLAY ANYMORE.

525
00:21:28,370 --> 00:21:29,705
WOULD YOU...?

526
00:21:29,747 --> 00:21:31,582
CAN YOU FINISH MY SET?

527
00:21:31,624 --> 00:21:33,918
AFTER THAT? YEAH!

528
00:21:35,169 --> 00:21:37,588
NO, I MEAN, IF I CAN HELP.

529
00:21:37,630 --> 00:21:38,881
YEAH.

530
00:21:43,427 --> 00:21:46,430
YEAH, LIKE, I COULD LOSE IT.

531
00:21:48,099 --> 00:21:49,142
WHAT?

532
00:21:49,183 --> 00:21:52,061
I PLAYED BAD ON PURPOSE, GUYS.

533
00:21:52,103 --> 00:21:53,646
OH!
OH!

534
00:21:53,687 --> 00:21:56,732
OKAY, SO, YOU WERE
TRYING TO PLAY BAD
THIS WHOLE TIME?

535
00:21:56,774 --> 00:21:58,651
NO, JUST THAT LAST SONG.

536
00:21:58,692 --> 00:22:01,570
[Captioned by
The Caption Center
WGBH Educational Foundation]

